Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 16:02:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08030/11362] Nothing reverted from 0cb1f23f3: half the vc33
 regression was a confound, the other half is a tradeoff a revert would not
 fix

REVERTED: nothing. KEPT from 0cb1f23f3: everything -- all five input-side
win-state fixes, the three corrections where the win-state change had been
penalising CORRECT predicates and had killed GOAL-REPAIR, and the gate changes
(root-true rejection, _model_candidates, the engine_calls budget unit). No
production code changed in this pass.

vc33, before -> after this commit: 15 -> 15. Unchanged, because nothing
changed. The reported "10" is the asset-ABSENT configuration, not production.
The ACTIONS regression is a measurement confound: the pre-flight ran every
base arm from a /tmp git worktree and every head arm from the canonical
checkout, and two live assets are gitignored so `git worktree add` does not
materialise them (results/experiment_4629_live_frame_change_cnn.pt, 2026-06-23;
data/arc_transition_corpus/*.npz, 2026-07-17 -- both predating the span under
test). Without them StepwiseExplorer builds no ActionEffectExpansionPrior and
the frontier expands in a different order. A balanced 4-commit x 2-asset grid,
run this pass because the first grid varied the commit only in the asset-free
arm: cfca5de95, e5ac4244d, 0cb1f23f3 and HEAD each give 15 with the assets and
10 without, with byte-identical traces. The commit axis is inert in BOTH asset
conditions. vc33's traces diverge at action 4, six actions upstream of the
level-up that fires its only induction, so no goal-predicate change could have
reached the number.

ka59: gate pass SURVIVES, unchanged -- and is NOT affordable. Reachable only at
max_nodes=160000 (137,347 nodes, plan_length 11, ~193-197 s/attempt against a
9.74 s non-LLM per-game budget). At the SHIPPED max_nodes=20000 the gate still
returns degenerate_goal_predicate with no plan.

BUG or TRADEOFF: a TRADEOFF, and NOT a pure win. The actions half is neither --
it is a confound. But the other half of the same report is real and
commit-caused: vc33's n_plans_found went 1 -> 0, refinement_rounds_used 1 -> 3,
cell wall 137.2 s -> 428.5 s. Replaying a FIXED captured predicate through each
commit's gate involves no path channel, and the p2 probe's root-true predicate
is satisfiable under e5ac4244d and rejected goal_predicate_true_at_root under
0cb1f23f3 and HEAD. So 0cb1f23f3 cost vc33 a real in-production plan and bought
ka59 a gate pass that cannot be paid for at the shipped budget. The first
version of this work said "the vc33 cost is disproved, nothing to weigh it
against" and closed G3 on that; that premise is withdrawn and G3 is reopened,
though still not taken (changing a budget UNIT to make a gate pass is the same
lower-the-bar class, and it is verdict-neutral for vc33).

It is still not reverted because recovering vc33's length-1 plan requires
re-admitting a predicate that is true at the root -- the p2 base arm's is a
literal `return True`. No quality gate was widened or disabled:
degenerate_goal_predicate, goal_predicate_true_at_root and min_heldout_accuracy
are untouched.

Review findings applied (each re-verified here, not taken on trust): the corpus
sweep's "11 of 12 identical" was false -- it compared three summary fields and
never hashed the trace; 8 of 12 diverge, 7 of them while every summary metric
ties, so the cost on tn36/tr87/cd82/tu93/ls20/cn04/r11l is unmeasured, not zero.
"Budget 40" overstated the depth: no cell reached it, all terminate at 25-26
actions. M2 kills TWO tests, not one (5/5 kill stands; the independence claim
did not). The `return True` quote came from the p2 probe, not the p3 arm that
produced the headline -- and the p3 base arm's persisted predicate is
degenerate under all three gate revisions including its own, yet recorded
satisfiable=true: an unexplained residual, recorded as such.

The real finding, not a regression: the live action-effect scorer costs +5
actions to first solve on vc33 (~56% of that level's score under
(baseline/agent)^2), pre-existing since 2026-06-23. One game, one seed.

Failure set: 136 affected files, 6 failed / 1330 passed, FAILED set line-for-line
identical to the pre-existing six. Neither original artifact edited (never-prune);
the correction cites both by sha256. No submission or scored/online ARC play.

